  "title": "Following Through With Boundaries",
  "content": "Setting boundaries is only half the work—following through is what makes them effective. Children test boundaries not because they are defiant, but because testing helps them understand where the limits truly are. When parents follow through calmly and consistently, children learn that boundaries are real and predictable.\n\nThis lesson helps parents understand why follow‑through is difficult, especially when they feel tired, stressed, or guilty. Parents learn how to stay steady without becoming harsh, and how to use natural and logical consequences instead of punishment.\n\nConsistency builds trust. When children know what to expect, they feel safer and behave more cooperatively.",
  "activities": [
    "Choose one boundary and practice following through every time for the next three days.",
    "Write down a calm, consistent response you will use when your child tests this boundary."
  ],
  "reflectionQuestions": [
    "What makes follow‑through challenging for you?",
    "How does your child react when you stay consistent?",
    "What support do you need to maintain boundaries during stressful moments?"
